      "title": "Where Things Are",
      "focus": "estar, hay, and locations",
      "estimated_minutes": 20,
      "objectives": [
        "say where a person or object is",
        "distinguish hay from está/están",
        "use en, aquí, and allí"
      ],
      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "Use 'es gibt' for “there is/there are” when introducing existence. Use 'sein' (ist/sind) for the location of a known singular or plural item.",
        "pattern": "Es gibt ein Buch auf dem Tisch. = There is a book on the table. Das Buch ist auf dem Tisch. = The book is on the table.",
        "contrast": "'Es gibt' introduces existence; 'sein' (ist/sind) locates."
      },
