      "teaching": {
        "explanation": "Short possessives come before the noun. German equivalents include 'mein' (my), 'dein' (your informal), 'sein/ihr/Ihr' (his/her/formal your), and 'unser' (our). In the nominative singular 'unser' becomes 'unsere' for feminine nouns: unsere Freundin.",
